\par 
Jung \emph{et al.} \cite{b9} proposed a method for scanning parking spaces by using laser-based radars. They developed a novel corner-detection strategy, including the detection of both rectangular and round corners, to enhance the detection accuracy. The high accuracy of a laser radar-based parking solution is remarkable, but the high cost of laser sensors limits the scalability of such systems.

