In the U.S.\ parking project SFpark \cite{bsf} by the San Francisco Municipal Transportation Agency, 8000 parking spaces were equipped with 11711 magnetometer sensors for periodically collecting and broadcasting information about the availability of parking spaces so that drivers can save time in cruising for parking spaces and congestion can be reduced.

