\subsection{Non-commutativity of the construction}\label{Sec4.2}

Recall that in the proof of \Cref{theorem2}, we started with $u\in\mathbb{H}(M_n)$ and took help of $w\in\mathbb{H}(M_n)$ to construct the nested sequence of vertex model subfactors
\[
\cdots \subset R^{u, w}_{k+1}\subset R^{u, w}_k\subset\cdots\subset R^{u, w}_0\subset R_u\subset R
\]
that have the Hadamard subfactor $R_u\subset R$ as an intermediate. Instead of this, if we start with $w$ and take the help of $u$ to construct the following nested sequence of vertex model subfactors
\[
\cdots \subset R^{w, u}_{k+1}\subset R^{w, u}_k\subset\cdots\subset R^{w, u}_0\subset R_w\subset R
\]
that have the Hadamard subfactor $R_w\subset R$ as an intermediate, then a natural question arises here whether $R^{u, w}_k\subset R$ are isomorphic to $R^{w, u}_k\subset R$ or not. This situation is depicted in \Cref{fig1}. This is exactly the question of noncommutativity of our construction.
