\subsection{Outline of the paper}

The paper is organized as follows. In Section \ref{sec2} we recall the BNP approach to the unseen-species problem, including the modeling assumptions and posterior inferences. Section \ref{sec3} contains the Gaussian CLT for $K_{m}^{(n)}$, with corresponding large $m$ asymptotic credible intervals for $K_{n,m}$. The empirical performance of our methodology is investigated in Section \ref{sec4}. Section \ref{sec5} concludes with a discussion and some directions for future research. Technical preliminary results, proofs and additional numerical illustrations are deferred to the Appendix.

