\paragraph{Non-Minimal Gapped Phases with Non-Minimal Symmetries.}
 We consider the non-minimal gapped phase with non-minimal symmetry corresponding to
\begin{equation}
A: \text{arbitrary}, \qquad B: \text{arbitrary}.
\end{equation}
We suppose that $A$ and $B$ are multiplicity-free.
As we discussed in section~\ref{sec: Non-Minimal Gapped Phases with Non-Minimal Symmetry}, the ground states of this gapped phase are given by
\begin{equation}
