\subsection{Agent Objectives}
\label{subsec:agent_objectives}

Each agent $i$ seeks to learn a policy $\pi_i$ that maximizes its long-term expected discounted reward:
\begin{equation}
\max_{\pi_i} \ \mathbb{E}_{\pi_i} \left[ \sum_{t=1}^{T} \gamma^{t-1} R_i(t) \right],
\end{equation}
where $\gamma \in [0,1]$ is a temporal discount factor.

The reward function balances three institutional goals:
\begin{equation}
R_i(t) = \text{Profit}_i(t) - \lambda \cdot \text{CVaR}_{\alpha}(X_i(t)) + \gamma_{\text{eff}} \cdot \text{Efficiency}_i(t),
\end{equation}
with:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \item $\text{Profit}_i(t)$: Underwriting result (premium - claims - commissions).
    \item $\text{CVaR}_{\alpha}$: Tail risk of the portfolio (95\% default).
    \item $\text{Efficiency}_i(t)$: Operational score.
\end{itemize}

\paragraph{Efficiency Metric:}
\[
\text{Efficiency}_i(t) = w_1 \cdot \text{WinRate}_i + w_2 \cdot \text{InvLatency}_i + w_3 \cdot \text{CostScore}_i, \quad \sum w_j = 1.
\]
\textit{Interpretation:} Agents are incentivized to bid quickly and competitively, simulating real-world underwriting discipline.

\paragraph{Loss Ratio (Monitoring Metric):}
\begin{equation}
\text{LossRatio}_i = \frac{\text{Claims Paid}_i}{\text{Premium Earned}_i},
\end{equation}
A solvency indicator widely used in insurance.

