\section{Results and Analysis}
\label{sec:results_analysis}

This section presents the empirical evaluation of our multi-agent reinforcement learning (MARL) framework for reinsurance treaty bidding. We benchmark its performance across profitability, risk mitigation, strategic competitiveness, and robustness under uncertainty. Our results demonstrate that MARL agents consistently outperform traditional approaches with statistically significant improvements and demonstrate resilience under realistic market stress.

