\subsection{Risk-Return Tradeoff Adaptation}
\label{subsec:risk_return_frontier_analysis}

Training agents with varying CVaR regularization weights ($\lambda$) produces a smooth Pareto frontier between expected profit and downside risk, shown in Figure~\ref{fig:risk_return_frontier}. As $\lambda$ increases from 0.1 to 10, average profit declines from 10.1 to 7.2, while CVaR\textsubscript{95\%} improves from 0.23 to 0.13.

\noindent
This tradeoff enables MARL agents to align with institutional risk preferences, adapting seamlessly from aggressive to conservative strategies. Vertical error bars reflect tight variability across five random seeds, confirming convergence reliability.

