\subsection*{Summary of Findings}

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Profitability}: 36.8\% higher average reward than actuarial baseline
    \item \textbf{Risk Mitigation}: 22.7\% lower CVaR\textsubscript{95\%}; adaptive to $\lambda$
    \item \textbf{Convergence}: Stable reward variance ($\sigma = 5.4$) across seeds
    \item \textbf{Robustness}: Converges across hyperparameters ($p < 10^{-39}$)
    \item \textbf{Stress Resilience}: Post-shock recovery rate = +0.224 (catastrophe), significant at $p < 10^{-190}$
\end{itemize}

These findings validate MARL as a powerful tool for dynamic, data-driven reinsurance treaty pricing and placement. It improves underwriting decisions, enhances risk-adjusted returns, and adapts robustly to volatile markets.

