\section{Learning Curve Diagnostics}
\label{appendix:learning_diagnostics}

To assess the convergence and stability of our MARL training framework, we analyze episodic reward variance and perform ablation tests across alternative learning configurations. These diagnostics complement the learning curves presented in Figure~\ref{fig:learning_curve} and provide further support for the robustness of centralized training with decentralized execution (CTDE)~\cite{lowe2017multi, yu2021surprising}.

Figure~\ref{fig:reward_variance_comparison} plots the reward variance across 10,000 episodes. Initially, MARL agents exhibit high variability due to exploration and the inherent non-stationarity of multi-agent environments. However, as training progresses, variance declines steadily---dropping below 100 by episode 10,000. In contrast, random bidding agents maintain flat, low-level variance throughout, reflecting a lack of adaptation and policy improvement.

