    &\left.+\log^{2}k\hspace{1mm}\zeta(0,\alpha/k)\zeta(0,\beta/k)\right].\label{F(0)exp}
\end{align}
If $0<a<1$, then the series in \eqref{zetaexp} converges uniformly and thus defines a continuous function for all real $\sigma\leq 0$. By continuity, \eqref{zetaexp} remains valid for $s=0$ also. Thus, we obtain
