\begin{comment}


However, the stock market is a complex and dynamic environment and there are several obstacles that need to be overcome to achieve this goal.
First, the high dimensionality of stock market data poses a challenge as a vast amount of data is generated on a daily basis, making it crucial to effectively process and analyze this data to extract useful insights \citep{cong2020alphaportfolio}. 
Second, the return patterns, price dynamics and risks in the market are always non-stationary \citep{fama1965investigations, park2011herding, salahuddin2020timevarying}, further complicates the task of making accurate predictions across the time. 
Third, the high noise-to-signal ratio in the stock market \citep{chong2020noisemarket,skyle1993noisemarket} makes it challenging to dig instructive market information and accurately predict future trends. 
Traditional predict-then-optimize approaches can propagate errors and lead to suboptimal trading decisions. 
