\subsection{Dynamic Embedding for Market State Space}\label{sec:dynamic embedding}



In the previous section, we introduce a framework capable of modeling the trading of a small group of stocks at a specific frequency, but its computational demands increase when trading a large number of stocks. Three major challenges contribute to this difficulty: high dimensionality, low signal-to-noise ratio and market nonstationarity.

