\begin{comment}
KL divergence is advantageous in financial data embedding as it enforces a constraint that the encoded distribution is close to a normal distribution, ensuring that the encoded states are well-behaved and can be effectively used in the reinforcement learning algorithm. On the other hand, MMD is advantageous in detecting differences between distributions that may not be captured by KL divergence, which is important in financial data embedding where the distribution of financial data may have complex features not well-captured by simple normal distributions. MMD may also be more robust to outliers in financial data, which is advantageous in applications where outliers are prevalent. The training procedures for both VAE and WAE are provided in Algorithm \ref{alg:VAE} and the E-Companion, respectively.

