For each large pre-trained weight matrix $W$ with size $p\times q$, LoRA freezes $W$ and replace it by $W+\Delta W$. Here $\Delta W=(\text{LoRA-}\alpha/r)AB$, where the trainable $A$ has size $p \times r$, and the trainable $B$ has size $r\times q$. The total number of trainable parameters decreases from $pq$ to $(p+q)r$, since $r\ll p,q$. The scaling factor $\text{LoRA-}\alpha$ controls the update rate.

