\subsection{Model Architecture}
\label{sec:3.4}

The model architecture diagram is shown in Figure \ref{fig:modelarchitecture}. In the figure, we can see that the social features are normalized; this is done to get a range of values that is reasonable in order to prevent data loss. The textual data is converted into vector representation using embeddings. 
%in order for each word to be analyzed. 
The image is also converted to RGB color model for classification models. Overall, an early fusion approach is taken whereby the combinations of modalities are done. As seen in Figure \ref{fig:modelarchitecture}, all the input features are concatenated in a fully connected layer before classification is done, indicating an early fusion approach. If the late fusion approach was to be taken, each of the input features would be independently classified and then the outputs from those classifiers would be concatenated in a later layer to be again classified to get the final output.  

For evaluation of classification results under different combinations of data type, precision, recall, and F1-score are used. Results of different settings are compared using these scores. 

