\subsection{Symbol Error Probability}

Once the decision threshold is determined, the symbol error probability \( P_e \) can be analyzed. The error probability is expressed as:
\[
P_e = P(b=0) P(\hat{b}=1 | b=0) + P(b=1) P(\hat{b}=0 | b=1).
\]

Assuming equi-probable bits, \( P(b=0) = P(b=1) = \frac{1}{2} \). When \( b = 0 \), \( X_t = X_0 \), and \( y_t(n) \sim \mathrm{Pois}(\lambda_0(n)) \), a false alarm occurs ($f$) if \( \hat{b} \) is decoded as \( 1 \). This happens when at least \( K \) out of the \( N \) values of \( y_t(n) \) exceed the threshold \( \xi_n \). Similarly, a miss detection ($m$) occurs when \( b = 1 \), \( X_t = X_1 \), and \( y_t(n) \sim \mathrm{Pois}(\lambda_1(n)) \), if \( {b} \) is decoded as \( 0 \). This happens when the number of '$1$' decisions are less than $K$.
%This happens when at least \( K \) values of \( y_t(n) \) do not exceed the threshold \( \xi_n \). Thus:
\begin{align*}
f = \mathbf{P} \bigg[ & \sum_n \mathbf{1} \big(\mathrm{Pois}(\lambda_0(n)) > \xi_n \big) \geq K \bigg]\\
%\\ & + \mathbf{P} \bigg[ \sum_n \mathbf{1} \big(\mathrm{Pois}(\lambda_0(n)) < \xi_n \big) < K \bigg].
m = \mathbf{P} \bigg[ & \sum_n \mathbf{1} \big(\mathrm{Pois}(\lambda_1(n)) > \xi_n \big) < K \bigg]
%\\ & + \mathbf{P} \bigg[ \sum_n \mathbf{1} \big(\mathrm{Pois}(\lambda_1(n)) > \xi_n \big) \geq K \bigg].
\end{align*}
For an AND combining rule (\( K = N \)):
\begin{align*}
    f &= \prod_{n=1}^N P\left[\mathrm{Pois}(\lambda_0(n)) > \xi_n \right], \\
    m &= \prod_{n=1}^N P\left[\mathrm{Pois}(\lambda_1(n)) < \xi_n \right].
\end{align*}
%\[
%f = \prod_{n=1}^N P\left[\mathrm{Pois}(\lambda_0(n)) > \xi_n \right], \text{ m =} \prod_{n=1}^N P\left[\mathrm{Pois}(\lambda_1(n)) < \xi_n\right]
%\]

The error probability becomes:
\begin{multline}
    P_e = \frac{1}{2} \bigg\{ 
    \prod_{n=1}^N \bigg(1 - e^{-\lambda_0(n)} \sum_{j=0}^{\xi_n} \frac{\lambda_0(n)^j}{j!} \bigg) \\
    + \prod_{n=1}^N \bigg(e^{-\lambda_1(n)} \sum_{j=0}^{\xi_n} \frac{\lambda_1(n)^j}{j!} \bigg) 
    \bigg\}.
\end{multline} % Fine-tune spacing after figures

