\section{Generalization to QCD}\label{sec:generalization_to_QCD}
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
The generalizations of the orbifold lattice Hamiltonian and orbifold lattice action to QCD are provided in ref.~\cite{Bergner:2024qjl}. They are designed so that the Kogut-Susskind Hamiltonian and Wilson action (with quarks) are obtained if $\det U_{j,\vec{n}}$ and $W_{j,\vec{n}}$ are set to 1 and the identity matrix $\textbf{1}_N$, respectively. This is achieved by adding the same additional term $\Delta\hat{H}$ or $\Delta S_{\rm orbifold}$ and sending the mass parameters $m^2$ and $m^2_{\rm U(1)}$ to infinity. 


